  Parity details:
    - Bound through the pure ElevationProfileProjection (samples + currentIndex +
      distanceUnit -> render-ready Display) over IElevationProfileSource; the view
      performs NO HTTP. gain/loss accumulation mirrors the web elevGain memo
      (positive deltas -> gain, |negative| -> loss, rounded); cursor resolution
      mirrors the web cursorDistance memo (in-range index -> distance, else null);
      distanceUnit falls back to "km" like the web default.
    - Click -> index: a tap maps to the nearest sample and the view-model raises the
      sample's ORIGINAL index on IndexSelected — the native analogue of the web
      onClickIndex(data[idx].index); out-of-range positions are ignored (web guard).
    - The chart is drawn inside the shared TsChartContainer (the native counterpart of
      the web ChartContainer) from the shared ChartGeometry / ChartShapes / ChartBrushes
      primitives (the same toolkit TsElevationProfile is built on); the existing
      TsElevationProfile chart primitive is intentionally NOT modified (out of the
      allowed cone and lacks the cursor + click parity needs). TsChartDataView is
      populated as a collapsed-by-default, screen-reader-friendly WinUI grid — the
      native accessible-table affordance; the web's chart-a11y:no-table opt-out is a
      recharts-SVG-table concern, not a "never offer data" mandate.
    - i18n: every string resolves through the P1/S10 facade with the web keys
